1. Progressive Electricity Billing
1. Problem Statement
Develop a program that calculates a household electricity bill using progressive consumption slabs, a fixed charge,
a surcharge, and a rebate. It should also compare the current bill with the previous bill and flag an unusual increase.

2. Objectives
•	Calculate energy charges using progressive slabs.
•	Add a fixed charge and apply a surcharge/rebate rule.
•	Compare bills and flag a significant increase.

3. Assumptions
•	Units are non-negative whole numbers.
•	Rates: first 100 units ₹1.50/unit; next 100 ₹2.50/unit; units above 200 ₹4.00/unit.
•	Fixed charge is ₹50. A 5% surcharge applies when consumption exceeds 250 units; otherwise no surcharge.
•	An unusual increase means the current bill is more than 25% above the previous bill.

4. Algorithm
1. Read current and previous units.
2. Calculate slab-wise energy charges.
3. Add fixed charge and apply the surcharge condition.
4. Calculate the previous bill using the same rules.
5. Compare bills and print the result.

